186060991 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186060564 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186060565 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186060564 #edb/ref 1061 143403 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186060564 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e2eb4f41-af42-517b-80cc-4e15c689de2d" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186060564 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186059697 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186060565 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186060566 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186060565 #edb/ref 1061 143406 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186060565 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c85a942c-f9af-53b4-b1da-fa03e8854a2d" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186060565 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186059698 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186060566 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186060567 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186060566 #edb/ref 1061 143409 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186060566 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a0cda17a-d96e-5ea8-bb9e-ccd79d7904dc" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186060566 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186059699 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186060567 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186060568 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186060567 #edb/ref 1061 143412 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186060567 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "74a00ea0-ef35-56ab-86b6-44c08bc91491" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186060567 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186060992 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186060568 #edb/ref 1061 143413 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186060568 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f375663a-5188-59fe-b4e2-7d315657f509" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186060568 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186059700 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186060991 #edb/ref 1064 "A conditional statement $A \\Rightarrow B$ has three related logical forms:\n\n- the **converse:** $B \\Rightarrow A$\n- the **inverse:** $\\lnot A \\Rightarrow \\lnot B$\n- the **contrapositive:** $\\lnot B \\Rightarrow \\lnot A$\n\nFor example, consider the following true statement:\n\n$\\qquad$ If I am George Washington, then I am an American.\n\nHere, the antecedent is $A=$ \"I am George Washington,\" and the consequent is $B=$ \"I am an American.\"\n\n- The *converse* is \"If I am an American, then I am George Washington.\"\n- The *inverse* is \"If I am not George Washington, then I am not an American.\"\n- The *contrapositive* is \"If I am not an American, then I am not George Washington.\"\n\nAs we can see from the statements above, only the contrapositive is also true." #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186060991 #edb/ref 1065 7979 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186060991 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "f381549b-ee22-54fc-8819-f65677237a08" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186060991 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186060992 #edb/ref 1064 "In general, we have the following facts:\n\n- The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement: $$\\underbrace{A \\Rightarrow B}_{\\textrm{original}} \\equiv \\underbrace{\\neg B \\Rightarrow \\neg A}_{\\textrm{contrapositive}}$$\n- The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other but not to the original statement: $$\\underbrace{\\neg A \\Rightarrow \\neg B}_{\\textrm{inverse}} \\equiv \\underbrace{B \\Rightarrow A}_{\\textrm{converse}}$$\n\nWe can prove these results using a truth table, as shown below:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\, A \\Rightarrow B \\,$ | $\\, \\neg A \\Rightarrow \\neg B \\,$ | $\\, B \\Rightarrow A \\,$ | $\\, \\neg B \\Rightarrow \\neg A \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{red} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{red} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ | $\\color{red} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{red} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{red} \\textrm F$ | $\\color{red} \\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{red} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{red} \\textrm T$ | $\\color{blue} \\textrm T$ |\n\nThis can be visualized using the following diagram.\n\n![](images/d9/d946d2a81d46cbde934ebbab54f9b69b514092e02da4f8a3b79768f218929449.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186060992 #edb/ref 1065 7980 #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186060992 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "5bbcfb96-5707-521a-bea1-559cf154472f" #edb/ref 17592186045585] [17592186060992 #edb/ref 1067 "Logically Equivalent Conditional Statements" #edb/ref 17592186045585]}
